---
import translationAfter from "../../captures/translation-after.png";
import translationPopup from "../../captures/translation-popup.png";
import translator from "../../captures/translator.png";
import Callout from "../../guide/Callout.astro";
import GuidePage from "../../guide/GuidePage.astro";
import Path from "../../guide/Path.astro";
import Task from "../../guide/Task.astro";
---

<GuidePage
  slug="translation"
  lead="Katari finds the text on a comic page and translates it. Text recognition always runs on the phone; with the right engine, translation does too."
>
  <Task id="engine" title="Pick a translation engine">
    <p>Choose one under <Path>Settings › Translation › Translation engine</Path>, and the language to translate into under <strong>Target language</strong>.</p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Engine</th> <th>Runs</th> <th>What it needs</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Android System Translation</strong></td> <td>On the phone</td> <td>Android 12 or newer</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Offline Translator</strong></td> <td>On the phone</td> <td>The Offline Translator app, set up as below</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>DeepL-compatible server</strong></td> <td>Over the network</td> <td>A server URL, and an API key for DeepL's own</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>LibreTranslate Server</strong></td> <td>Over the network</td> <td>A server URL, and an API key if the server asks</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>The <strong>Playground</strong> on the same screen tries the engine on text you type.</p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="offline-translator" title="Set up Offline Translator">
    <ol>
      <li>Install Offline Translator from F-Droid and download its language models.</li>
      <li>In Offline Translator, enable its HTTP API and bind it to localhost.</li>
      <li>In Katari, pick <strong>Offline Translator</strong> as the engine, confirm the <strong>HTTP API port</strong> (5000 unless you changed it), and tap <strong>Test connection</strong>.</li>
    </ol>
  </Task>

  <Task id="page" title="Translate a comic page" shot={{ image: translationAfter, alt: "A comic page with its speech bubbles translated into English", caption: "Translations on the page" }}>
    <ol>
      <li>In the reader, tap <strong>Translate text</strong> in the bottom bar. A translation bar opens above it.</li>
      <li>
        The first time, the bar asks what it needs: <strong>Which language is the text in?</strong>, how to read that language, and the
        models to download. Answer each with its button.
      </li>
      <li>Once the bar says <strong>Tap a speech bubble to translate it</strong>, tap one.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      <strong>Show translations on the page</strong> in the bar draws every bubble's translation over the page. <strong>Select area</strong>
      translates text you drag over, for writing outside the bubbles.
    </p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="bubble" title="Hear a bubble read aloud" shot={{ image: translationPopup, alt: "One speech bubble's translation with buttons to hear it read aloud", caption: "One bubble" }}>
    <p>
      A tapped bubble shows its translation beside the original. <strong>Listen to original</strong> and <strong>Listen to translation</strong>
      read either one with the phone's text-to-speech voices.
    </p>
    <p>
      Pick the voice and its pitch under <Path>Settings › Text to speech</Path>, and try them in its <strong>Speech playground</strong>. A voice
      that runs over the network asks first, with <strong>Use network voice?</strong>
    </p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="text-recognition" title="Choose how text is recognized">
    <p>Katari reads the page with models it downloads once and keeps on the phone. The bar picks them by the page's language:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Japanese manga</strong> finds the bubbles with the comic text and bubble detector and reads them with Manga OCR, vertical text and furigana included.</li>
      <li><strong>Comics</strong> in other scripts read their bubbles with PaddleOCR.</li>
      <li><strong>Comics with ML Kit</strong> uses Google's text recognition instead.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <Path>Settings › Text recognition</Path> changes the engine and the choice per language, lists <strong>Downloaded models</strong> with
      their size, and has a playground for trying a picture.
    </p>
    <Callout label="Mobile data" tone="warning">
      <p>
        Models only download over Wi-Fi or another unmetered network unless you tick <strong>Allow download over mobile data</strong> in
        <strong>Download models?</strong> Otherwise the download stops at <strong>Waiting for a non-metered network</strong>; start it again
        with the box ticked, or on Wi-Fi.
      </p>
    </Callout>
    <Callout label="Katari FOSS">
      <p>ML Kit needs Google Play services, so Katari FOSS leaves it out. The on-device models are in both builds.</p>
    </Callout>
  </Task>

  <Task id="series" title="Keep a series' languages">
    <p>
      Tap the language chip in the translation bar to open <strong>Languages for this series</strong>. <strong>Page language</strong> and
      <strong>Translate to</strong> stay with the series; changing the page language reads its pages again. <strong>Translate downloads</strong>
      translates the series' chapters in the background once they're downloaded.
    </p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="chapters" title="Translate whole chapters ahead">
    <ol>
      <li>On a title's page, long-press chapters to select them and tap <strong>Translate</strong>.</li>
      <li><strong>Before translating</strong> lists anything still missing, each with a button to fix it. Then tap <strong>Translate</strong>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Under <Path>Settings › Downloads › Auto-translate</Path>, Katari can translate new chapters as they download and translate ahead while you read:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Translate new items</strong> works together with <strong>Download new items</strong>.</li>
      <li><strong>Translate ahead while viewing</strong> keeps the next few chapters ready.</li>
      <li><strong>Only on Wi-Fi</strong> is on from the start; <strong>Only while charging</strong> is off.</li>
    </ul>
  </Task>

  <Task id="translator" title="Translate typed text" shot={{ image: translator, alt: "The Translator turning a line of Japanese into English", caption: "The Translator" }}>
    <p>
      The <strong>Translator</strong> tab translates anything you type or paste, with <strong>Detect language</strong> for text you can't
      place. It is hidden at first; add it under <Path>Settings › Appearance › Home screen tabs</Path>.
    </p>
    <p>In books, select text to get <strong>Listen</strong> and <strong>Translate</strong> for that passage.</p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="backups" title="What carries over to another phone">
    <p>
      Backups keep the engine, target language, voices and text recognition choices with each profile. They leave out server addresses
      and API keys, which stay on this phone, and the models, which download again when a page needs them.
    </p>
  </Task>
</GuidePage>
